From cc24ebb8fe9148c3b63f327c785c1e5efd61e21e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:17:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Unwrap an agent host's reported directory before matching
 it to a folder

A dev-container window listed no sessions at all. The host reports each
session's working directories wrapped for the agent-host filesystem
(`vscode-agent-host://b64-<host address>/workspace/repo`), while the
window's folder is `vscode-remote://dev-container+<hex>/workspace/repo`.
`isEqualOrParent` compares schemes before anything else, so the two never
match and every session is filtered out.

The wrapper carries the original URI in its `_ah` query, and unwrapping it
yields the very `vscode-remote:` URI the window uses for that folder, so
the comparison is exact. Measured in a live dev-container window: the
unwrapped authority equals the folder's, byte for byte.

That also answers what the scheme rewrite alone could not. Rewriting a
`file:` directory into the folder's namespace has to assume the window's
remote is the session's host, since a bare path carries no host identity.
The unwrapped URI carries it, so a directory on a different remote is
correctly rejected rather than adopted. The rewrite stays as the fallback
for a host that does report a bare `file:` path.

The matching predicate is now exported so the tests exercise it rather
than a replica of it.
